            <ArticleTitle>Wound pain: a challenge for the patient and the wound care specialist.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-20; quiz 21-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To provide physicians and nurses with an overview of the mechanisms, pathophysiology, assessment, and treatment of pain related to pressure ulcers.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="TARGET AUDIENCE" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">This continuing education activity is intended for physicians and nurses with an interest in learning about management of patients with pressure ulcer-related pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="LEARNING OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">After reading the article and taking the test, the participant will be able to: 1. Describe the mechanisms and pathophysiology of pain related to pressure ulcers. 2. Identify assessment parameters and treatment options for pain related to pressure ulcers.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
